analysisWe need to output an assert statement matching the comment:

"@@@ If the element is not null, then the array contains the added element after the operation"

We need to use publicly accessible observer methods: contains(Object o) is available. So after add, if element != null, then this.contains(element) holds.

But we also have precondition that element is not null (the method throws if null). So we can assert that element != null => this.contains(element). However given method throws NullPointerException if element null, the postcondition only needs to assert that after operation, the array contains the added element. Since null case can't happen (exception), we can assert simply this.contains(element). But to be safe, we can include implication: element != null => this.contains(element). Use element variable.

Thus final answer:

<code>assert element != null => this.contains(element);</code>

Check syntax: need parentheses maybe because => lower precedence than && etc. Not needed. Provide as code block.

